MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T04:39:01Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T04:40:05Z","body":"I used the Secret Rabit Code for VoIP, so could it be exposed somehow? I would be thrilled, but it can be another PR.\r\n\r\nGodot has significant issues with sample rate conversion for microphone inputs vs speaker sample rate.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495305142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495471749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2495471749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2495471749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UveCF","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T12:58:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T15:59:34Z","body":"I did a few production builds to check the size penalty.\r\n\r\nThe approximate results:\r\n|Method|Increase|\r\n|-|-|\r\n|Sinc Fast|24.31 KiB|\r\n|Sinc Medium|100.31 KiB|\r\n|Sinc Best|1.31 MiB|\r\n\r\nNote, however, that `libsamplerate` is only being applied on editor builds, for this importer. Size increases tend to be a concern on template builds mostly.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, either Medium or Best should be the one used. While Fast is slightly better than the current Cubic, I think it's better to sacrifice a few more KiBs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495471749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495529468","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2495529468","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2495529468,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UvsH8","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T16:22:59Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T16:23:52Z","body":"Sinc Medium is probably the right compromise here, considering a 1+ MB increase is very significant for mobile and especially the web editor (it directly impacts its startup times).\r\n\r\nImport speeds also matter for ease of iteration, and Sinc Medium should import files much faster than Sinc Best too. I'd be surprised if the difference can be heard in a double blind test either way :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495529468/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495535830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2495535830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2495535830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UvtrW","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T16:44:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T21:55:29Z","body":"> I'd be surprised if the difference can be heard in a double blind test either way 🙂\r\n\r\nBy doing a blind shootout test between the three Sinc modes with a high-frequency heavy audio, I ended up picking Medium most of the times. Fast turned to be the most noticeable (and worst, obviously).\r\n\r\nConsidering the audio won't be upsampled using a heavy algorithm anyway, Medium really seems to be the best choice.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495535830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495547422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2495547422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2495547422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uvwge","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co