rate code to work in the runtime templates for my use in problems like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99930 and voip, but use your best judgment.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517485453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517689002","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2517689002","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2517689002,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WEOKq","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T15:02:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T15:02:59Z","body":"Is there a way that each platform could define the quality needed for Sinc? It could be even exposed to the user at compile time. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517689002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518034383","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2518034383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2518034383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WFifP","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T17:01:47Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T17:01:47Z","body":"> Is there a way that each platform could define the quality needed for Sinc? It could be even exposed to the user at compile time.\r\n\r\nEach Sinc quality is locked behind a define, so you could just swap them. Although I think Fast isn't that much of an improvement compared to Cubic (and it's much heavier).\r\n\r\nAs this is an import procedure, I think consistency between platforms should be respected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518034383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518202589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2518202589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2518202589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WGLjd","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T18:19:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T18:19:48Z","body":"> As this is an import procedure, I think consistency between platforms should be respected.\r\n\r\nMaybe. But we should at least set a SCons parameter of the chosen quality, with medium as default.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518202589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2519152261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2519152261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2519152261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WJzaF","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T05:11:15Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T14:21:39Z","body":"Added a `builtin_libsamplerate` variable to allow it to be provided by the system.\r\n\r\nChecks failing to find `samplerate.h`, weird since it builds fine in my system. What did I do wrong?\r\n\r\n**Edit: Solved. I have to be more careful with prepends.**","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2519152261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524826072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2524826072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2524826072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WfcnY","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T02:55:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T02:57:07Z","body":"> > As this is an import procedure, I think consistency between platforms should be respected.\r\n> \r\n> Maybe. But we should at least set a SCons parameter of the chosen quality, with medium as default.\r\n\r\n\r\nI'm honestly against exposing the other Sinc methods because:\r\n1. Sinc Best provides little benefit over Sinc Medium considering the additional import time, size penalty and, although not really an issue, git diff.\r\n2. Sinc Fastest isn't much better than Godot's built-in Cubic, which is a much faster method. Another case of little benefit.\r\n3. Some applications like sndfile-resample and LMMS are set to use Sinc Medium by default, despite providing both Sinc Best and Sinc Fastest as options. Godot isn't a software focused in audio, so I think it should go with the most \"default\" option.\r\n\r\nIf there is support, however, I would 100% add the other options. But as it is at the time of this writing, someone that **really** needs Sinc Best or Sinc Fastest could just drop the header for it in the folder, then change two lines of code (the define exposing the respective Sinc method and the method used AudioStreamWAV).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2524826072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555512677","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2555512677","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2555512677,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YUgdl","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T18:29:08Z","updated_at":"2024-12-19T22:38:38Z","body":"I was experimenting this PR with a few different sounds, and I noticed a significant difference in a specific one.\r\n\r\nThe following was taken from the TPS Demo, specifically the robot explosion sound:\r\n\r\n[samplerate.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34a98f03-8eca-4753-8489-a49c3a9fbb35)\r\n\r\nAll sounds above (apart from the original) were saved using Godot's save_to_wav function.\r\n\r\nOn Cubic, you can notice a high frequency sound at the beginning that you can't hear on Sinc Medium or Sinc Best (or even Sinc Fastest, but it muffles so much that I removed it from the equation). The sound is also noticeable in libsamplerate's Linear and ZOH converters.\r\n\r\nTo some extent, I think it's accurate to say this PR fixes something now, but only from the editor's side.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2555512677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692813942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2692813942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2692813942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ggRR2","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T16:53:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T16:54:22Z","body":"Why only WAV files? Shouldn't the new resampling be applied for all formats?\r\n\r\nI'm also curious to see a visual comparison between Fast, Medium, and Best. https://src.infinitewave.ca/ has graphs for Best, but not Fast or Medium. Some of their testing methodology is documented [here](https://src.infinitewave.ca/help.html).\r\n\r\nDo we have benchmarks for DSP processing time when we have, say, a hundred audio sources playing at once? If there's noticeable performance impact we should consider exposing this as a project setting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692813942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692821449","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2692821449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2692821449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ggTHJ","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T17:11:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T17:11:39Z","body":">  samplerate.webm \r\n> All sounds above (apart from the original) were saved using Godot's save_to_wav function.\r\n\r\nThanks for the demo! I decided to make a quick spectrogram:\r\n\r\n![TPS_Demo_Spectrogram](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95dae8ef-523a-4afc-a618-de6997712350)\r\n\r\nYou can definitely see the aliasing in Cubic around 10khz. Sinc Medium seems to cut off the very high frequencies around 15.5khz, but this is probably unnoticeable to a lot of people.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692821449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692827491","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2692827491","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2692827491,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ggUlj","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T17:28:18Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T17:35:08Z","body":"> Why only WAV files? Shouldn't the new resampling be applied for all formats?\r\n\r\nBecause it only affects WAV loading/importing, which has a resampling process. Not playback, which uses a simple linear interpolation.\r\n\r\nOgg Vorbis and MP3 files are imported as they are.\r\n\r\nIf you're looking for a PR that improves WAV playback resampling, that would be #100652","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692827491/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692839507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2692839507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2692839507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ggXhT","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T18:03:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T18:03:07Z","body":"Yeah, I was thinking resampling during playback. Sounds like that's work for a separate PR then.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692839507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692851772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99572#issuecomment-2692851772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99572","id":2692851772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ggag8","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T18:36:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T18:39:12Z","body":"Could you run some tests with the files here and output WAV files for analysis, or just provide a spectrogram of the sweep? https://src.infinitewave.ca/TestSignals.zip\r\n\r\nThe test in question involves resampling from 96k to 44.1k.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692851772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]